course: dictionary
lesson: 13878
title: One word, three meanings: kiosk
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The clues around it tell you which meaning fits. The word is kiosk, and it can mean a small stand, a machine, or an old word for a phone box.
explain: «We bought an ice cream at the kiosk in the park.» Ice cream is sold here, and the kiosk is a small stand. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "We bought an ice cream at the small stand in the park" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «Press the screen to pay at the kiosk, then collect your ticket.» Press, screen and pay are the clues. Here a kiosk is a machine that you use yourself, not a person or a shop.
fact: A kiosk is a small hut or stand where things like newspapers, snacks, drinks or tickets are sold.
fact: A kiosk can also be a machine with a screen in a public place, where you buy tickets, pay or get information.
fact: In older British English, a kiosk could mean a phone box.
fact: Common phrases with kiosk are ice-cream kiosk, ticket kiosk and self-service kiosk.
fact: Kiosk is a noun. One is a kiosk, and more than one is kiosks.
exercise: «We bought an ice cream at the kiosk in the park.» What is a kiosk in this sentence? | A kind of bird | *A small stand where things are sold | A large house in a garden | A bus stop
exercise: «Please buy your ticket at the ticket kiosk on the platform.» What can you do at a ticket kiosk? | Grow vegetables | *Buy a ticket | Sleep for the night | Swim in a pool
exercise: A kiosk sells juice boxes for 2 pounds each. How much do 3 juice boxes cost? | 5 pounds | 12 pounds | 9 pounds | *6 pounds
test: «Press the screen on the self-service kiosk to pay.» What is a self-service kiosk? | A person who sells ice cream | A kind of bus | *A machine with a screen where you pay | A tall tree in the park
test: In older British English, what could a kiosk mean? | A type of cake | A horse's stable | A sandwich | *A phone box
exam: Which sentence uses kiosk to mean a machine with a screen? | «The kiosk sells hot dogs by the lake.» | «We sat on the kiosk to rest.» | «The kiosk was full of cold drinks.» | *«Scan your ticket at the kiosk, then press Start.»
